{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC AMENDMENT — the removal-mirroring criteria are RETIRED, and what replaces them\n\nOperator ruling applied: research the ecosystem, build if it is a parity gap, defer if it is not\ncommonly handled. The research (previous comment) found it is NOT commonly handled. So the ACs written\naround \"the removal IS emitted\" no longer describe what this ticket ships, and pretending otherwise\nwould leave a permanently-red live cell and a ticket whose criteria can never be ticked.\n\n**RETIRED** (they specify a feature deliberately not shipped — recorded, not silently dropped):\n * a link deleted in Jira is mirrored locally / the local dep is positively absent after the pass\n * the removal record survives the apply layer end to end\n * G1 observed-empty EMITS the removal; G2/G3/G4/G5 gating of that removal\n * the live cell `test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips` is GREEN on a harness run\n * \"the mutation set MUST include making the removal unconditional\"\n\n**WHAT THIS TICKET ACTUALLY SHIPPED, and what now stands as its criteria:**\n - [x] the apply-layer DROP is fixed. `apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links` used to\n       discard any non-`add` link record outright (`action != \"add\": continue`), so even a correct\n       differ could not have worked. That branch + the `rebar.unlink` wiring landed in 1276 and is\n       independently mutation-proven. This was a REAL defect and it is fixed.\n - [x] G1/G2/G3/G5 landed and are mutation-proven. They are dormant (nothing emits a removal for them\n       to gate) but they are correct, and they are the guards a future implementation needs.\n - [x] the shipped semantics are STATED: local-wins-and-restore. A link deleted in Jira is re-added on\n       the next pass — convergent, no local data destroyed, identical on both backends.\n - [x] the live cell is XFAIL with the full reason in the marker (change 1303), NOT inverted and NOT\n       deleted, so it fails loudly as an xpass the moment a removal path starts working.\n - [x] the ecosystem evidence is recorded, with sources, so this is not re-litigated from scratch.\n - [x] **the refutation of the original design is recorded, with a probe** — `managed_refs` cannot\n       distinguish \"a link we never pushed\" from \"a link the peer deleted\"; the two states are\n       IDENTICAL on every input the guards read. That is the finding that stopped a second data-loss\n       defect before it was written.\n - [x] **the correct design is recorded WITH A WORKING TEMPLATE.** Change 1296 landed exactly this\n       pattern for parents — a per-binding record of what the peer last had, advanced only on\n       OBSERVATION — so whoever picks this up starts from shipped, reviewed code rather than from the\n       refuted premise. `binding_store` is already a parameter of both link differs, so no new differ\n       parameter is needed.\n\n**WHY THIS IS NOT \"AMENDING AWAY AN INCONVENIENT AC\".** The distinction the operator drew on 5200's\nrow 12 was: do not amend away a COVERAGE gap. This is not that. The cell exists and still runs; what\nchanged is the product decision about what behaviour to ship, taken on ecosystem evidence plus a\nfirst-hand incident in which the identical inference destroyed 63 parent edges. The behaviour is\ndocumented rather than quietly absent, and the loud-on-xpass marker means a future fix cannot land\nunnoticed.\n\n**RESIDUAL RISK, stated plainly:** a link deleted in Jira comes back. A user who deletes a link in Jira\nand does not also unlink locally will see it reappear. That is a real divergence from user intent, it is\nNOT DC-specific, and it is the behaviour every comparable tool in this space also ships.\n\nCloses when 1303 lands."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785776534971535001,"uuid":"9d3c5cb0-93b6-4e62-8be6-be05d29b930b"}